{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/borrowingiteratorprotocol\/nextspan(maximumcount:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol"]]},"metadata":{"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","name":"iPadOS"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0","deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","deprecated":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS"},{"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false}],"externalID":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP8nextSpan12maximumCounts0E0Vy7ElementQzGSi_tF","title":"nextSpan(maximumCount:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","required":true,"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nextSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"maximumCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a span over the next group of elements that are ready to by visited,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"up to the specifed maximum.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/nextSpan(maximumCount:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@_lifetime(&self) @_lifetime(self: copy self) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nextSpan"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maximumCount"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"Span","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:s25BorrowingIteratorProtocolP7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the underlying type stores its elements in one or more blocks of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contiguous memory, then the returned span typically directly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"addresses one of those buffers. On the other hand, if the underlying type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"materializes its elements on demand, then the returned span addresses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a temporary buffer managed by the iterator itself. Consequently, the returned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"span is tied to this particular invocation of ","type":"text"},{"code":"nextSpan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and it cannot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"survive beyond the next invocation of this method.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the iterator has not yet reached the end of the underlying elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then this method returns a non-empty span of at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements and updates the iterator’s current position to the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following the last item in the returned span. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument allows callers to avoid getting more items than they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"able to process in one go, simplifying usage, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"avoiding materializing more elements than needed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the iterator’s current position is at the end of the container, then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this method returns an empty span without updating the position.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This method can be used to efficiently process the items of a container","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in bulk, by directly iterating over its piecewise contiguous pieces of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var it = items.makeBorrowingIterator()","while true {","  let span = it.nextSpan(maximumCount: .max)","  if span.isEmpty { break }","  \/\/ Process items in `span`","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The spans returned by this method are not guaranteed to be disjunct.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iterators that materialize elements on demand typically reuse the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer over and over again; and even some proper containers may link to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single storage chunk (or parts of a storage chunk) multiple times, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example to repeat their contents.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}],"identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","type":"image","alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background."},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Int":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Int"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/int","abstract":[{"text":"A signed integer value type.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Int","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Int"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/BorrowingIteratorProtocol/nextSpan(maximumCount:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a span over the next group of elements that are ready to by visited,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"up to the specifed maximum."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/borrowingiteratorprotocol\/nextspan(maximumcount:)","title":"nextSpan(maximumCount:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BorrowingIteratorProtocol\/nextSpan(maximumCount:)","required":true,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nextSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumCount","ki